<title>SWEDEN: Swedish Nov c/a surplus 6.3 bln crowns.</title>
<headline>Swedish Nov c/a surplus 6.3 bln crowns.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sweden's current account for November showed a surplus of 6.3 billion crowns for a surplus of 43.9 billion in the previous 12 months, Sweden's central bank, the Riksbank, said on Monday.  </p>
<p> SWEDISH CURRENT ACCOUNT	 Nov 96    Oct 96   Nov 95</p>
<p> Monthly balance		   +6.3	+6.7     +4.9</p>
<p> Year/year			  +43.9     +42.5    +35.0</p>
<p>Note - Figures are in billions of crowns. Average market expectations had been for a 6.0 billion crown surplus.</p>
<p>-- Abigail Schmelz, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1003</p>
</text>
